# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <div v-for="count in 5"></div>
  <div v-for="helper in 5"></div>
  <div v-for="size in 5"></div>
  <div v-for="props in 5"></div>
  <div v-for="modelValue in 5"></div>
</template>

<script setup>
import { helper } from "./helper.js";

let count = 42;
const props = defineProps({ size: Number });
const value = defineModel();
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidScriptSetup.vue:3:15 lint/nursery/noVueTemplateShadow ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The template variable count hides a variable with the same name.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <div v-for="count in 5"></div>
      │               ^^^^^
    4 │   <div v-for="helper in 5"></div>
    5 │   <div v-for="size in 5"></div>
  
  i The hidden count is declared here.
  
    11 │ import { helper } from "./helper.js";
    12 │ 
  > 13 │ let count = 42;
       │     ^^^^^
    14 │ const props = defineProps({ size: Number });
    15 │ const value = defineModel();
  
  i Inside this element, count refers to the template variable, so the other count can't be used, and the two are easy to confuse.
  
  i Rename the template variable.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

